Action Steps:
1. Identify why moving workflows from Make.com to Active Pieces is beneficial, focusing on the increased token allocation; 
2. Categorize and list workflows that are suitable for migration based on complexity and compatibility; 
3. Document existing automations in Make.com, detailing their functionalities; 
4. Compare the apps and integrations available in Make.com and Active Pieces to understand limitations; 
5. Create folders in Active Pieces and name them appropriately for migrated workflows; 
6. Simplify the migration process by focusing on simpler workflows that can be efficiently transferred; 
7. Use Airtable triggers and OpenAI as an example of creating a new flow in Active Pieces; 
8. Enhance prompts where applicable to improve automation efficiency; 
9. Thoroughly document the migrated workflows, marking completed migrations as done; 
10. Prioritize moving workflows that are actively in use, ignoring inactive ones.

